    {
      "id": "claim_4917449c61fe4989812230eabbfe0428",
      "statement": "template_plan() walks goals in priority order, greedily selecting one cue-ready habit per uncovered goal within max_active and available_minutes. Weak links are allowed only when no stronger cue-ready alternative is left unpicked, so weak links never block dedicated habits. Chosen habits are deduplicated by ID.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/habitquest_backend/catalog/scoring.py#L79-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c074618a3ff62ce39c6008ad0813a3fe12fa57396abec4e80ed764604d825deb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_36ec52f9c45b4f00b40091ce37edde67",
      "statement": "The template plan marks unresolved goals with one of four reason codes: needs_cue (no routine cue configured), no_catalog_entry (no habit serves the goal), deferred (active-habit cap or minutes exceeded), or paused (parent explicitly pauses the goal in the LLM selection).",
      "evidence": [
